<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31977" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκηλος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκᾱλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>at rest, at
				one's ease,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> esp. of persons feasting and enjoying themselves, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δὲ ἕκηλοι τέρπονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.759
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκηλος πῖνε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					21.309
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκηλοι νεκροὺς ἂμ πεδίον
				συλήσετε</span> ye will plunder them <i>at your ease,</i>
			i.e. <i>without let</i> or <i>hindrance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.70
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκηλος ἐρρέτω</span> let him
			be off <i>in peace,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				9.376
			</span></i> ; of mere inaction, <i>quiet,</i> only twice in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσθἰ ἕκηλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.478
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκηλοι κάτθετε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					21.259
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.100
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκαλος ἔπειμι γῆρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					7(6).41
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕ. εὕδειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					769
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐᾶν ἕκηλόν τινα</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				826
			</span></i> : neut. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκηλα ἡμερεύειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>El.</u>
					786
				</span></i>
			 : metaph. of a field, <i>lying at rest</i> or <i>fallow,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Cer.
				451
			</span></i> ; of trees, <i>unmoved,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.969
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
